          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Ganita Manjari | Grade 9 | Part I"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.132,
            0.115,
            0.398,
            0.138
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Think and Reflect"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.128,
            0.152,
            0.867,
            0.192
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Predict the number of squares in the next three stages of the pattern and write the sequence of numbers up to Stage 7 of the pattern."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.113,
            0.207,
            0.884,
            0.248
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Each stage is obtained by adding two more tiles to the previous stage. The table mentions the number of tiles for the first seven stages."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.117,
            0.259,
            0.883,
            0.36
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "table_body",
              "index": 5,
              "bbox": [
                0.117,
                0.259,
                0.883,
                0.36
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_6_table_5.jpg",
              "content": "<table><tbody><tr><td>Stage</td><td>1</td><td>2</td><td>3</td><td>4</td><td>5</td><td>6</td><td>7</td></tr><tr><td>Number of the square tiles</td><td>1</td><td>3</td><td>5</td><td>7</td><td>9</td><td>11</td><td>13</td></tr></tbody></table>"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.112,
            0.367,
            0.886,
            0.445
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "To generalise this pattern, we observe that the number of squares at each stage is one less than twice the number of the term. For example, in Term 2, the number of squares is "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "2 \\times 2 - 1 = 3"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " , in Term 5, the number of squares is 2 × 5 – 1 = 9 and so on."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.112,
            0.445,
            0.885,
            0.483
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "This leads us to conclude that the number of squares at Stage n is given by 2n – 1."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.483,
            0.886,
            0.602
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "The polynomial 2n – 1 has degree 1. Hence, it is an example of a linear polynomial. Also, the difference between consecutive terms in the sequence of the number of squares, that is, 1, 3, 5, 7, 9 … is the constant value 2. Thus, with each stage, the number of squares increases by 2. The relationship between the number of the stage and the number of square tiles is a "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "linear relationship",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.132,
            0.629,
            0.399,
            0.653
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Think and Reflect"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.128,
            0.666,
            0.868,
            0.724
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Using the expression 2n – 1, can you find out how many tiles will be there in the 15th stage and the 26th stage of the pattern? Also, which stage will contain 21 tiles and 47 tiles?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.113,
            0.745,
            0.885,
            0.787
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Example 7:",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Bela has `100 for pocket money. She spends `5 every day. After how many days will she be left with `40?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.117,
            0.802,
            0.883,
            0.896
          ],
          "content": [
